'''Paul Pratt''' (born May 1, 1985) is an American former professional [[American football|football]] player who was a [[cornerback]] for the [[Detroit Lions]] of the [[National Football League]] (NFL).<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |title=Paul Pratt |url=https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/P/PratPa20.htm |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211117174033/https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/P/PratPa20.htm |archive-date=2021-11-17 |access-date=2023-04-17 |website=Pro-Football-Reference.com |language=en}}</ref><ref>{{cite news | url=https://www.newspapers.com/article/detroit-free-press/163674257/ | title=From L.A. Fitness to Detroit's secondary | work=[[Detroit Free Press]] | date=August 27, 2010 | accessdate=22 January 2025}}</ref> He played [[college football]] for the [[Nevada Wolf Pack football|Nevada Wolf Pack]].<ref name=":0" /> He was signed by the [[New York Sentinels]] as a [[street free agent]] in 2009.{{Citation needed|date=April 2023}}
